# DjiMatrice (DJI Matrice 300 RTK) on ArduCopter, loaded after ArduPilot's default_params/copter.parm.
# BiguaSim model: dynamics.uav.QuadCopterX, 6.3 kg, rotors 0..353 rad/s, thrust k_eta w^2 (176.9 N in all).

# Quad X. The bridge sends MOT1..4 (SERVO1..4) to the front-right, back-left, front-left and back-right rotors.
FRAME_CLASS     1
FRAME_TYPE      1

# The bridge maps 1000..2000 us linearly to 0..353 rad/s: the thrust grows with the square of the output.
MOT_PWM_MIN     1000
MOT_PWM_MAX     2000
MOT_THST_EXPO   1.0
MOT_SPIN_ARM    0.05
MOT_SPIN_MIN    0.08
MOT_SPIN_MAX    1.0
# Hover at 6.3 kg: 61.8 N of the 176.9 N, 35 %
MOT_THST_HOVER  0.35
MOT_HOVER_LEARN 2

# One IMU sample per physics step (200 Hz): ArduPilot wants them at 1.8 x its loop rate or more.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 100

# Rate gains: ArduCopter's defaults suit a ~1.5 kg quad; the Matrice has ~5x its torque per inertia and with them
# the rotors swung between minimum and 300 rad/s every few ticks. Offline (OfflineWorld) at 200 Hz: hover steady
# within 0.25 deg, a 15 m step in 4.4 s with 0.13 m overshoot.
ATC_RAT_RLL_P   0.04
ATC_RAT_RLL_I   0.04
ATC_RAT_RLL_D   0.001
ATC_RAT_PIT_P   0.04
ATC_RAT_PIT_I   0.04
ATC_RAT_PIT_D   0.001
